mtp2otf 1.7
===========
Convert MathTime(TM) Professional 2 Type 1 fonts to OpenType MATH.
Use TTF on Windows and OTF with LuaLaTeX.

Full provides cv01-cv19 and ss01-ss10. Lite provides cv01-cv09, ss07
and ss10, with the same meanings. All selectors are off by default.

doc/mtp2otf-guide.pdf describes how to use the fonts, and
doc/mtp2otf.pdf how to build them and the design of the font.

Requirements
------------
POSIX shell, Python 3.10+ with fontTools, and tx from the Adobe Font
Development Kit for OpenType (AFDKO). Commands must be on PATH.
Debian and Ubuntu install tx in /usr/libexec/afdko; run, for example,
PATH="/usr/libexec/afdko:$PATH" ./build.sh

Inputs
------
Create mtpro2/ and donor/ beside build.sh and supply fonts separately.
mtpro2/: MTPro2 PFB/TFM files and mtpro2.sty. Full also needs
umt2ms.fd, umt2mf.fd, umt2bb.fd and umt2hrb.fd. Checked with
mtpro2.sty 2009/4/27 v2.3; other releases are untested.
donor/: NimbusRoman-Regular.otf from Artifex urw-base35, or another
static upright Roman font given with -d. TeX Gyre Termes, URW Times
and Monotype Times New Roman have also been tried.

Build
-----
  ./build.sh                 Full
  ./build.sh -l              Lite
  ./build.sh -d FILE         use FILE as the Roman donor
  ./build.sh -h              usage
  ./build.sh -V              version

Output in out/:
  Full: MTPro2Math.otf, MTPro2Math.ttf
  Lite: MTPro2MathLite.otf, MTPro2MathLite.ttf

Before building, every input file, glyph slot, fontdimen and donor
character the build uses is checked; any shortage stops the build with
a list of what is missing. The build is silent when it succeeds.
Errors go to stderr; the exit status is 0 on success, 1 for a problem
with the inputs or the environment and 2 for a usage error.

build/<edition>/ (full or lite) holds build.log, which records the
inputs and outputs, and tab-separated tables of the values the build
computed from the inputs: constants.tsv, glyphs.tsv, variants.tsv,
parts.tsv, features.tsv, kerns.tsv and dictionaries.tsv. See
doc/mtp2otf.pdf for their columns.

The fonts are for the licensee's own use; do not redistribute them.
They may be embedded in documents.

Documentation
-------------
Build the fonts first; then, in doc/,
  lualatex mtp2otf-guide.tex (twice)
  lualatex mtp2otf.tex       (twice)
The documents use Nimbus Roman and Nimbus Mono PS as installed fonts
and ../out/MTPro2Math.otf.

Files
-----
  build.sh                   Entry point; runs tools/mtp2otf.py.
  VERSION                    Version number.
  tools/                     Converter: sources/ (reading the inputs),
                             design/ (reading the design data), plan/
                             (computing the font), emit/ (writing the
                             fonts and the tables).
  tools/data/                Design data (tab-separated tables).
  doc/                       Documentation (LaTeX sources and PDF).
  LICENSE                    0BSD for project code and documentation.

Font and dependency licenses apply separately.
